SUMMARY:CSA Triangle October Meet-Up | Governing Agentic Work
DESCRIPTION:Cloud Security Alliance Triangle Chapter\n**Governing Agentic 
 Work: An Open Architecture for AI Workforce Adoption**\n\n**Summary of Pre
 sentation:**\nMoving beyond AI chatbots means trusting agents to build app
 lications\, reach internal systems\, and run repeatable workflows. That tr
 ust cannot be granted with a long-lived API key. In this session\, Johnnie
  Tabron draws on Cloudflare's own internal experience and the newly open-s
 ourced Cloudflare OS architecture to show what it actually takes to put ag
 ents to work safely.\n\nAttendees will see how organizational context and 
 reusable skills keep agents aligned to established terminology\, procedure
 s\, and standards\, and how a conversation becomes an editable document\, 
 a connected application\, and a mostly deterministic workflow. They will a
 lso learn why capability-based access beats handing credentials to agents 
 and generated code. From there\, the talk walks through the governance lay
 er that constrains agent authority\, controls where observed data moves\, 
 and preserves human accountability\, before showing how every step gets ce
 ntralized oversight and how agents finally ship as isolated\, full-stack a
 pplications that any organization can deploy and customize in its own Clou
 dflare account.\n\nBenefits-led but security-focused\, the session's centr
 al message is that useful enterprise AI demands more than controlling the 
 first model or tool call. Designed for security leaders\, architects\, clo
 ud and platform engineers\, developers\, GRC professionals\, and AI practi
 tioners\, the talk is presented through diagrams\, architecture visuals\, 
 and interface examples\, followed by Q&A.
